    <h1>Privacy Policy for Elements to Everything</h1>
    <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 10, 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>
        Welcome to Elements to Everything ("the Game"), developed by Mediu ("we," "our," or "us").
        We respect your privacy and aim to be transparent about how information may be processed when you use the Game.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Information We Process</h2>

    <h3>2.1 Game Progress and Local Data</h3>
    <p>
        The Game stores gameplay progress on your device. This may include information such as discovered items,
        game progress, hint-related values, settings, and other gameplay state needed for the Game to function.
    </p>

    <h3>2.2 Google Play Games Services</h3>
    <p>
        The Game may use Google Play Games Services for features such as authentication, player services,
        and cloud save / saved game functionality. Information handled by Google Play Games Services is processed
        according to Google's own privacy policies and terms.
    </p>

    <h3>2.3 In-App Purchases</h3>
    <p>
        The Game may offer in-app purchases. Payments are processed by Google Play.
        We do not receive or store your full payment card or billing details.
        We may receive purchase status or entitlement information needed to provide purchased content.
    </p>

    <h3>2.4 Advertising</h3>
    <p>
        The Game may display advertisements using Google AdMob.
        AdMob may process information such as device identifiers, advertising identifiers,
        IP address, device information, and ad interaction data in accordance with Google's policies.
    </p>

    <h2>3. How Information Is Used</h2>
    <p>Information may be used for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Providing and maintaining gameplay functionality</li>
        <li>Saving and restoring game progress</li>
        <li>Providing Google Play Games features</li>
        <li>Processing and restoring in-app purchases</li>
        <li>Displaying advertisements</li>
        <li>Preventing fraud, abuse, and unauthorized manipulation of game data</li>
        <li>Diagnosing technical issues and improving stability</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>The Game may use the following third-party services:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Play Services / Google Play Games Services</strong> — authentication, player services, and saved game functionality</li>
        <li><strong>Google Play Billing</strong> — processing in-app purchases</li>
        <li><strong>Google AdMob</strong> — serving advertisements</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        These third-party providers may process information under their own privacy policies.
        We encourage you to review Google's privacy information for details about how Google processes data.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Advertising and Consent</h2>
    <p>
        The Game may show ads through Google AdMob. Depending on your region, device settings, age eligibility,
        and applicable consent requirements, ads may be personalized or non-personalized.
        Where required, consent choices may be presented before certain advertising data is used.
    </p>
    <p>
        The Game may also offer an in-app purchase that removes certain advertising placements.
        Optional rewarded ads may still remain available where applicable.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data Storage, Backup, and Security</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Game progress is stored locally on your device.</li>
        <li>Game progress may also be backed up or restored through supported Android backup mechanisms.</li>
        <li>If Google Play Games Saved Games is enabled, progress may also be stored or synchronized through Google services.</li>
        <li>We use technical measures intended to protect game save data from accidental corruption and unauthorized modification.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
        The Game is not intended to knowingly collect personal information directly from children.
        Third-party services used by the Game may apply age-appropriate protections and consent requirements
        according to applicable law and platform policies.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you are a parent or guardian and believe that personal information has been provided inappropriately,
        please contact us using the information below.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Your Choices and Rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights regarding personal data processed by third-party services.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>You can uninstall the Game to remove locally stored game data from your device.</li>
        <li>You can manage advertising and privacy settings through your device and Google account settings.</li>
        <li>You can contact us with privacy-related questions or requests.</li>
        <li>Google account and Google Play Games data may be managed through the relevant Google services and settings.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
        Local game progress remains on your device until it is deleted, cleared, or removed according to device behavior.
        Data processed by Google or other third-party services is retained according to those providers' own policies.
    </p>

    <h2>10. International Data Processing</h2>
    <p>
        Third-party service providers such as Google may process information on servers located in different countries.
        Their processing is governed by their own privacy policies and applicable legal safeguards.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time.
        When we do, we will update the "Last Updated" date at the top of this page.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us:</p>
    <p><strong>Email:</strong> mdikeroglugame@gmail.com</p>
